# Mrs. Tuppence — Chesburg's cat lady; her cat Biscuit is missing. Format: dialogue/dialogue_parser.gd
@speaker Mrs. Tuppence
@when tuppence_got_cat -> after
@when cat_found -> found
@when tuppence_quest_accepted -> reminder

== offer ==
Oh, thank goodness, a friendly face! Have you seen a cat? Orange, round, [i]very[/i] sure of himself. Answers to "Biscuit", though he's never once answered.
He slipped out yesterday morning and hasn't come home. My knees won't carry me around the whole town, but yours look [bounce]splendid[/bounce].
Would you look for him? He leaves little... [i]traces[/i] wherever he goes.
> I'll find Biscuit. -> accepted [set tuppence_quest_accepted]
> Sorry, I'm busy. -> no

== no ==
Oh. Well. If you see an orange loaf with legs, [whisper]do let me know.[/whisper]

== accepted ==
Bless you, dear! Cats leave clues like crumbs. Orange fur on a fence, muddy paws near the well, something nicked from the baker's... Look where a cat would look.

== reminder ==
Any word of Biscuit? Try the places a cat likes: fur on the fences by the road, paw prints near the well, and whatever he's stolen from Marta's kitchen.
> Not yet, I'm still looking.

== found ==
Is that — oh, [bounce]Biscuit![/bounce] He's been trotting behind you this whole time! [shake]You wicked, wicked boy.[/shake]
Thank you, dear. Truly. Here, take this. He'll be sulking by the stove all week, [whisper]but he's home.[/whisper] [set tuppence_got_cat]

== after ==
Biscuit hasn't left the cushion since. Thank you again, dear.
